  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "The Dodgers took the lead early and the Padres never fully reclaimed it, leaving runners on base at the moments that mattered most.",
    "what_this_means": "Manny Machado carried the offense with a two-run homer, enough to keep them in a game that felt winnable through six innings. But two separate runners-in-scoring-position situations. One in the fourth, one in the seventh. Produced nothing. The bullpen held after Canning exited with three runs in five innings, but holding wasn't enough when the bats couldn't finish. This is what fragile looks like: one run separating them from taking the series, but that one run is the whole story. They scored twice. They needed three. That gap is the only thing that matters right now.",
